msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grover's algorithm description"
msgstr "Deskripsi algoritma Grover"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description of Grover's algorithm {#description-of-grovers-algorithm}"
msgstr "Deskripsi algoritma Grover {#description-of-grovers-algorithm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we'll describe Grover's algorithm.\n"
"We'll begin by discussing *phase query gates* and how to build them, followed by the description of Grover's algorithm itself.\n"
"Finally, we'll briefly discuss how this algorithm is naturally applied to searching.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di bagian ini, kita akan mendeskripsikan algoritma Grover.\n"
"Kita akan mulai dengan mendiskusikan *Gate query fase* dan cara membuatnya, diikuti dengan deskripsi algoritma Grover itu sendiri.\n"
"Terakhir, kita akan secara singkat mendiskusikan bagaimana algoritma ini secara alami diterapkan untuk pencarian.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase query gates {#phase-query-gates}"
msgstr "Gate query fase {#phase-query-gates}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Grover's algorithm makes use of operations known as *phase query gates*.\n"
"In contrast to an ordinary query gate $U_f$, defined for a given function $f$ in the usual way described previously, a phase query gate for the function $f$ is defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Grover menggunakan operasi yang dikenal sebagai *Gate query fase*.\n"
"Berbeda dengan Gate query biasa $U_f$, yang didefinisikan untuk fungsi $f$ tertentu dengan cara biasa yang dijelaskan sebelumnya, Gate query fase untuk fungsi $f$ didefinisikan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert x\\rangle = (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_f \\vert x\\rangle = (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr "untuk setiap string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operation $Z_f$ can be implemented using one query gate $U_f$ as this diagram suggests:\n"
msgstr "Operasi $Z_f$ bisa diimplementasikan menggunakan satu Gate query $U_f$ seperti yang disarankan diagram ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit implementing a Z_f gate using one query gate together with the phase kickback phenomenon](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Z_f.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Circuit kuantum yang mengimplementasikan Gate Z_f menggunakan satu Gate query bersama dengan fenomena phase kickback](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Z_f.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implementation makes use of the phase kickback phenomenon, and requires that one workspace qubit, initialized to a $\\vert -\\rangle$ state, is made available.\n"
"This qubit remains in the $\\vert - \\rangle$ state after the implementation has completed, and can be reused (to implement subsequent $Z_f$ gates, for instance) or simply discarded.\n"
msgstr ""
"Implementasi ini memanfaatkan fenomena phase kickback, dan membutuhkan satu qubit ruang kerja, diinisialisasi ke state $\\vert -\\rangle$, untuk tersedia.\n"
"Qubit ini tetap dalam state $\\vert - \\rangle$ setelah implementasi selesai, dan bisa digunakan kembali (untuk mengimplementasikan Gate $Z_f$ berikutnya, misalnya) atau sekadar dibuang.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the operation $Z_f$, we will also make use of a phase query gate for the $n$-bit OR function, which is defined as follows for each string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr "Selain operasi $Z_f$, kita juga akan menggunakan Gate query fase untuk fungsi OR $n$-bit, yang didefinisikan sebagai berikut untuk setiap string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{OR}(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  0 & x = 0^n\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"  1 & x \\neq 0^n\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{OR}(x) =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  0 & x = 0^n\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"  1 & x \\neq 0^n\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explicitly, the phase query gate for the $n$-bit OR function operates like this:\n"
msgstr "Secara eksplisit, Gate query fase untuk fungsi OR $n$-bit beroperasi seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"- \\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n.\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} \\vert x\\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\vert x\\rangle & x = 0^n \\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"- \\vert x\\rangle & x \\neq 0^n.\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To be clear, this is how $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ operates on standard basis states; its behavior on arbitrary states is determined from this expression by linearity.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memperjelas, inilah cara $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ beroperasi pada state basis standar; perilakunya pada state sembarang ditentukan dari ekspresi ini oleh linearitas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ can be implemented as a quantum circuit by beginning with a Boolean circuit for the OR function, then constructing a $U_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ operation (that is, a standard query gate for the $n$-bit OR function) using the procedure described in the *Quantum algorithmic foundations* lesson, and finally a $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ operation using the phase kickback phenomenon as described above.\n"
"Notice that the operation $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ has no dependence on the function $f$ and can therefore be implemented by a quantum circuit having no query gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ bisa diimplementasikan sebagai Circuit kuantum dengan dimulai dari Circuit Boolean untuk fungsi OR, kemudian membangun operasi $U_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ (yaitu, Gate query standar untuk fungsi OR $n$-bit) menggunakan prosedur yang dijelaskan di pelajaran *Quantum algorithmic foundations*, dan akhirnya operasi $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ menggunakan fenomena phase kickback seperti yang dijelaskan di atas.\n"
"Perhatikan bahwa operasi $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ tidak memiliki ketergantungan pada fungsi $f$ dan karenanya bisa diimplementasikan oleh Circuit kuantum yang tidak memiliki Gate query.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description of the algorithm {#description-of-the-algorithm}"
msgstr "Deskripsi algoritma {#description-of-the-algorithm}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have the two operations $Z_f$ and $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$, we can describe Grover's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita sudah memiliki dua operasi $Z_f$ dan $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$, kita bisa mendeskripsikan algoritma Grover.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The algorithm refers to a number $t$, which is the number of *iterations* it performs (and therefore the number of *queries* to the function $f$ it requires).\n"
"This number $t$ isn't specified by Grover's algorithm as we're describing it, and we'll discuss later in the lesson how it can be chosen.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma ini mengacu pada angka $t$, yaitu jumlah *iterasi* yang dilakukan (dan karenanya jumlah *query* ke fungsi $f$ yang diperlukan).\n"
"Angka $t$ ini tidak ditentukan oleh algoritma Grover seperti yang kita deskripsikan, dan kita akan membahas nanti dalam pelajaran bagaimana cara memilihnya.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Grover's algorithm\">\n"
"1. Initialize an $n$ qubit register $\\mathsf{Q}$ to the all-zero state $\\vert 0^n \\rangle$ and then apply a Hadamard operation to each qubit of $\\mathsf{Q}$.\n"
"2. Apply $t$ times the unitary operation $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ to the register $\\mathsf{Q}$\n"
"3. Measure the qubits of $\\mathsf{Q}$ with respect to standard basis measurements and output the resulting string.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Grover's algorithm\">\n"
"1. Inisialisasi register $n$ qubit $\\mathsf{Q}$ ke state all-zero $\\vert 0^n \\rangle$ lalu terapkan operasi Hadamard ke setiap qubit dari $\\mathsf{Q}$.\n"
"2. Terapkan $t$ kali operasi uniter $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ ke register $\\mathsf{Q}$\n"
"3. Ukur qubit-qubit dari $\\mathsf{Q}$ berdasarkan pengukuran basis standar dan keluarkan string yang dihasilkan.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ iterated in step 2 will be called the *Grover operation* throughout the remainder of this lesson.\n"
"Here is a quantum circuit representation of the Grover operation when $n=7\\!:$\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi $G = H^{\\otimes n} Z_{\\mathrm{OR}} H^{\\otimes n} Z_f$ yang diiterasi di langkah 2 akan disebut *operasi Grover* sepanjang sisa pelajaran ini.\n"
"Berikut adalah representasi Circuit kuantum dari operasi Grover ketika $n=7\\!:$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit representation of the Grover operation](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_operation.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Representasi Circuit kuantum dari operasi Grover](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_operation.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram, the $Z_f$ operation is depicted as being larger than $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ as an informal visual clue to suggest that it is likely to be the more costly operation.\n"
"In particular, when we're working within the query model, $Z_f$ requires one query while $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ requires no queries.\n"
"If instead we have a Boolean circuit for the function $f$, and then convert it to a quantum circuit for $Z_f$, we can reasonably expect that the resulting quantum circuit will be larger and more complicated than one for $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam diagram ini, operasi $Z_f$ digambarkan lebih besar dari $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ sebagai petunjuk visual informal untuk menyarankan bahwa operasi itu kemungkinan merupakan operasi yang lebih mahal biayanya.\n"
"Secara khusus, ketika kita bekerja dalam model query, $Z_f$ membutuhkan satu query sementara $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}$ tidak membutuhkan query.\n"
"Jika sebaliknya kita memiliki Circuit Boolean untuk fungsi $f,$ dan kemudian mengubahnya menjadi Circuit kuantum untuk $Z_f,$ kita bisa dengan wajar mengharapkan bahwa Circuit kuantum yang dihasilkan akan lebih besar dan lebih rumit dari satu untuk $Z_{\\mathrm{OR}}.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a diagram of a quantum circuit for the entire algorithm when $n=7$ and $t=3$.\n"
"For larger values of $t$ we can simply insert additional instances of the Grover operation immediately before the measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah diagram Circuit kuantum untuk seluruh algoritma ketika $n=7$ dan $t=3$.\n"
"Untuk nilai $t$ yang lebih besar kita cukup menyisipkan instance tambahan dari operasi Grover tepat sebelum pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit for Grover's algorithm when t=3](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Circuit kuantum untuk algoritma Grover ketika t=3](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/grover-algorithm/Grover_circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Application to search {#application-to-search}"
msgstr "Aplikasi untuk pencarian {#application-to-search}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Grover's algorithm can be applied to the *Search* problem as follows:\n"
msgstr "Algoritma Grover bisa diterapkan pada masalah *Search* sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the number $t$ in step 2. (This is discussed later in the lesson.)\n"
msgstr "Pilih angka $t$ di langkah 2. (Ini dibahas nanti dalam pelajaran.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run Grover's algorithm on the function $f$, using whatever choice we made for $t$, to obtain a string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan algoritma Grover pada fungsi $f$, menggunakan pilihan yang kita buat untuk $t$, untuk mendapatkan string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query the function $f$ on the string $x$ to see if it's a valid solution:\n"
msgstr "Query fungsi $f$ pada string $x$ untuk melihat apakah itu solusi yang valid:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $f(x) = 1$, then we have found a solution, so we can stop and output $x$.\n"
msgstr "Jika $f(x) = 1$, maka kita telah menemukan solusi, jadi kita bisa berhenti dan mengeluarkan $x$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Otherwise, if $f(x) = 0$, then we can either run the procedure again, possibly with a different choice for $t$, or we can decide to give up and output \"no solution.\"\n"
msgstr "Jika tidak, jika $f(x) = 0$, maka kita bisa menjalankan prosedur lagi, mungkin dengan pilihan berbeda untuk $t$, atau kita bisa memutuskan untuk menyerah dan mengeluarkan \"tidak ada solusi.\"\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we've analyzed how Grover's algorithm works, we'll see that by taking $t = O(\\sqrt{N})$, we obtain a solution to our search problem (if one exists) with high probability.\n"
msgstr "Setelah kita menganalisis bagaimana algoritma Grover bekerja, kita akan melihat bahwa dengan mengambil $t = O(\\sqrt{N})$, kita mendapatkan solusi untuk masalah pencarian kita (jika ada) dengan probabilitas tinggi.\n"
